<title>NEW ZEALAND: Guardian cuts NZ variable rate to 10.15 percent.</title>
<headline>Guardian cuts NZ variable rate to 10.15 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guardian Assurance has cut its variable mortgage rate to 10.15 percent from 10.85 percent, the New Zealand Press Association reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In a group bulletin published on Tuesday, Guardian said the new variable rate would come into effect from January 1 for existing customers not on the group's capped rate.</p>
<p>Guardian's two-year fixed rate falls to 8.95 percent from 10.25 percent and its one-year capped rate falls to 9.2 percent from 9.95 percent.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
